{
  "analysis": "The task requires merging and transforming data from three different sources (JSON, CSV, Parquet) with varying schemas and handling conflict resolution based on priority (A > B > C). Due to the complexity of schema mapping, data format handling (parquet, json, csv), and conflict tracking, a dedicated scripting language like Python, utilizing data processing libraries (e.g., pandas, pyarrow), is necessary. I will write a comprehensive Python script to execute this ETL workflow.",
  "plan": "1. Create a Python script (`merge_users.py`) that encapsulates the entire logic. 2. The script will load data from the three sources, mapping fields to standardized names ('user_id', 'email', 'name', 'created_date', 'status'). 3. It will iterate through records, merging them using 'user_id' as the key, and enforcing the priority rule (A > B > C) for conflict resolution. 4. During the merge, it will track any field value differences across sources to populate the conflict report. 5. Finally, it will save the merged dataset as Parquet and the conflict report as JSON to the specified paths.",
  "commands": [
